# Upgrading a CD-ROM Network for Multimedia Applications.

**Authors:** Sylvia, Margaret

## Abstract
Addresses issues to consider when upgrading library CD-ROM networks for multimedia applications. Topics includes security issues; workstation requirements such as soundboards and monitors; local area network configurations that avoid bottlenecks: Asynchronous Transfer Mode, Ethernet, and Integrated Services Digital Network; server performance bottlenecks; CD-ROM drives; and connection to the Internet. (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ508682

